# Review: SheetPlugin

The core is solid. `Sheet` is an ECHO type (`org.dxos.type.sheet` at 0.2.0) with sparse indexed cells,
ordered row and column indices, axis meta and a flat `ranges` array. `SheetModel` evaluates
formulas through HyperFormula and maps A1 references to indices. The axis ops are wired with undo
(`DropAxis` inverts to `RestoreAxis`). `ComputeGraphRegistry`, the markdown `ExtensionProvider`
and `AnchorSort` are contributed. The Playwright spec covers cell entry, SUM with a row deletion,
and range alignment. `sheet-model.test.ts` covers formulas and index mapping.

The spec lags the formatting model. A highlight is a `highlight` key whose value is a CSS colour,
alongside the `style` values `header`, `highlight` and `softwrap`. Comment overlays come from thread
anchors, not from `comment` ranges. `Range.range` holds an indexed range, not A1 notation.
`scrollToAnchor` takes `id`, not `ref`. None of the ops (`insertAxis`, `restoreAxis`,
`scrollToAnchor`, `create`) is invoked by a test, and nothing tests two-peer replication.

Of 43 items: 12 done, 15 untested, 9 partial, 3 diverged, 4 missing.

